esphome-xteink

The ESPHome glue in components/xteink/*.py, *.h, *.cpp is MIT licensed (see LICENSE).

components/xteink/dependencies/freeink is a pinned fork/submodule of the
FreeInk SDK (https://github.com/Free-Ink/freeink-sdk, MIT). Its LICENSE and NOTICE
remain in the submodule; the exact revision is in dependencies.json and the
Git gitlink. components/xteink/dependencies/rendering is the MIT-licensed
Xteink rendering/calibration library (https://github.com/morpheby/xteink-rendering).
FreeInk is itself derived from the OpenX4 E-Paper Community SDK
(https://github.com/open-x4-epaper/community-sdk, MIT); the SSD1677 driver and
panel waveforms originate with CidVonHighwind and that community.

The first ESPHome integration of these drivers was ngxson/esphome-component-xteink
(MIT), whose display/buttons/battery YAML shape this project keeps compatible.
